bDateTZ": "UTC", "fetched_at": "2026-08-15 15:31:39", "image_url": "https://assets.kooora.com/images/v3/getty-2215579826/crop/MM5DINRRGU5DENJZGY5G433XMU5DAORSGQ2A====/GettyImages-2215579826.jpg?auto=webp&format=jpg&quality=80", "video_url": null, "source_id": "kooora", "source_name": "\u0643\u0648\u0648\u0648\u0631\u0629", "source_priority": 4562, "source_url": "https://www.kooora.com", "source_icon": "https://n.bytvi.com/kooora.jpg", "sentiment": "ONLY AVAILABLE IN PROFESSIONAL AND CORPORATE PLANS", "sentiment_stats": "ONLY AVAILABLE IN PROFESSIONAL AND CORPORATE PLANS", "ai_tag": "ONLY AVAILABLE IN PROFESSIONAL AND CORPORATE PLANS", "ai_region": "ONLY AVAILABLE IN CORPORATE PLANS", "ai_org": "ONLY AVAILABLE IN CORPORATE PLANS", "ai_summary": "ONLY AVAILABLE IN PAID PLANS", "duplicate": false}, {"article_id": "065e2672005359e224edc2713187f25b", "link": "https://saudigazette.com.sa/article/663743/sports/al-hilal-beat-al-faisaly-4-2-as-ruben-neves-scores-twice-in-rsl-opener", "title": "Neves scores twice as Al Hilal survive Al Faisaly fightback in RSL opener", "description": "RIYADH \u2014 Ruben Neves scored twice from the penalty spot as Al Hilal survived a second-half fightback from newly promoted Al Faisaly to open their 2026-27 Roshn Saudi League campaign with a 4-2 victory on Friday.Karim Benzema opened the scoring from the penalty spot at Kingdom Arena before Neves converted another and Malcom tapped home to give Simone Inzaghi\u2019s side a commanding 3-0 lead at halftime.But Al Faisaly, back in the Saudi top flight for the first time since 2021, threatened a remarkable comeback with two goals in five minutes around the hour mark to cut the deficit to one.Al Hilal weathered the pressure before Neves converted his second penalty late on to secure all three points and complete his brace, earning the Portugal international the Man of the Match award.Despite the victory, Neves was critical of Al Hilal\u2019s second-half performance after the hosts allowed Al Faisaly back into a match they appeared to have under control.\u201cFirst 45 minutes, we just controlled all the game,\u201d Neves said. \u201cSecond half, we dropped a little bit the quality, we dropped a little bit the focus, and in this league, it's not allowed anymore.\u201d\u201cWe need to improve. We cannot concede two goals playing at home, winning 3-0, controlling all the game.\u201dAl Hilal entered the new campaign seeking to go one better after finishing runners-up to rivals Al Nassr in a dramatic 2025-26 title race despite going unbeaten throughout the league season.Neves acknowledged Al Hilal are still working toward peak condition following preseason but said taking three points from the opener was crucial.\u201cPhysically, we're still not in our best,\u201d he said. \u201cWe are coming from a lot of work in pre-season; we are finding now our best form. It's normal in the first games of the season.\u201cIt was important for us to get the three points. It was important to show that we can play like we played in the first half, because it was very good.\u201dFor Neves, the result represented the ideal start on paper, even if the performance left room for improvement.\u201cIn terms of points, yes, it's the perfect way to start: three points, four goals,\u201d he said. \u201cIn terms of performance, it's the perfect way to start like we did in the first half. Second half, we need to improve.\u201d", "content": "ONLY AVAILABLE IN PAID PLANS", "keywords": ["sports"], "creator": ["saudi gazette"], "language": "english", "country": ["saudi arabia"], "category": ["sports"], "datatype": "news", "pubDate": "2026-08-15 15:08:09", "pubDateTZ": "UTC", "fetched_at": "2026-08-15 15:16:18", "image_url": "https://saudigazette.com.sa/saudigazette/uploads/images/2026/08/15/2751010.webp", "video_url": null, "source_id": "saudigazette", "source_name": "Saudi Gazette", "source_priority": 356263, "source_url": "https://saudigazette.com.sa", "source_icon": "https://n.bytvi.com/saudi